{
  "comment": "NVDA-convention keybindings. VkCode values are Windows virtual key codes (the low-level hook reports left/right-specific modifier keys, e.g. 162/163 for Ctrl). Mode: Browse, Focus, or Any. The Insert modifier means the screen reader key (Insert or CapsLock per settings). Bound keys are swallowed unless passThrough is true. Browse- and Focus-mode bindings only apply while a web document has focus; outside documents only Any bindings apply. In Browse mode, unbound typing keys are swallowed so they can't trigger page shortcuts. Tab is not bound: it moves real focus in the browser and the virtual cursor follows focus. Numeric keypad keys (Num Lock off) have their own codes, as in NVDA's desktop layout: Numpad0-9 are 96-105, Numpad. is 110, Numpad- 109, Numpad* 106, Numpad/ 111 and Numpad Enter 269; an unbound keypad key works as the key it stands for (Numpad8 as Up); the plain keypad keys are the review cursor. With Num Lock on the keypad types digits.",
